{
  "sn16.10:0.1": "Linked Discourses 16.10 ",
  "sn16.10:0.2": "1. Kassapa ",
  "sn16.10:0.3": "The Nuns’ Quarters ",
  "sn16.10:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "sn16.10:1.2": "At one time Venerable Mahākassapa was staying near Sāvatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery. ",
  "sn16.10:1.3": "Then Venerable Ānanda robed up in the morning and, taking his bowl and robe, went to Mahākassapa and said, ",
  "sn16.10:1.4": "“Come, Honorable Kassapa. Let’s go to one of the nuns’ quarters.” ",
  "sn16.10:1.5": "“You go, Reverend Ānanda. You’re the one with many duties and responsibilities.” ",
  "sn16.10:1.6": "And a second time … ",
  "sn16.10:1.7": "",
  "sn16.10:1.8": "",
  "sn16.10:1.9": "And a third time, Ānanda said, ",
  "sn16.10:1.10": "“Come, Honorable Kassapa. Let’s go to one of the nuns’ quarters.” ",
  "sn16.10:2.1": "Then Venerable Mahākassapa robed up in the morning and, taking his bowl and robe, went with Venerable Ānanda as his second monk to one of the nuns’ quarters, where he sat down on the seat spread out. ",
  "sn16.10:2.2": "And then several nuns went up to Mahākassapa, bowed, and sat down to one side. ",
  "sn16.10:2.3": "Mahākassapa educated, encouraged, fired up, and inspired those nuns with a Dhamma talk, ",
  "sn16.10:2.4": "after which he rose from his seat and left. ",
  "sn16.10:3.1": "But the nun Thullatissā was upset and blurted out, ",
  "sn16.10:3.2": "“What is the venerable Mahākassapa thinking, that he’d teach Dhamma in fron